{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And he was to her a son.</b> Because she raised him in her house." "<b>And she called his name Moshe.</b> According to the words of our Sages, she converted and learned the holy tongue. After the miracle — that he was drawn from the water — to remind that he is of the Hebrews, and therefore he is not mentioned anywhere in the Torah except by this name. Another interpretation: Pharaoh's daughter did not know the holy tongue, but this is the plain sense of Scripture: <b>and she called</b> — Yocheved called his name Moshe; <b>and she said</b> — Pharaoh's daughter said to her: what does the word Moshe mean? And she told her that it is a term of drawing, and then Pharaoh's daughter said: you have named him well, for ״מן המים משיתהו״ (from the water I drew him). <b>Moshe.</b> It does not write here משוי, but rather משה, to say: just as I drew him, so shall he draw others — interpreted: he shall draw Israel out of Egypt."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:51.330570073Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}